stateDiagram-v2
  accTitle: Draining and forced cutoff are different outcomes
  accDescr: Ready service enters Draining after a handled stop trigger and admission is stopped. Completed owned work and cleanup permit local closure. A drain deadline can instead lead to forced cutoff with unfinished or unknown outcomes.
direction TB
  state "Locally closed" as Closed
  state "Deadline exceeded" as Expired
  state "Forced cutoff" as Forced
  Ready --> Draining : stop admission
  Draining --> Closed : drain / cleanup done
  Draining --> Expired : deadline
  Expired --> Forced : cut off
  classDef pending fill:#FFFBEB,stroke:#B45309,color:#111827;
  classDef success fill:#DCFCE7,stroke:#15803D,color:#111827;
  classDef failure fill:#FEE2E2,stroke:#B91C1C,color:#111827;
  class Draining,Expired pending
  class Closed success
  class Forced failure
